<font class="content">Written by <a href="">gugarko</a> on Tuesday, June 22 @  W. Europe Daylight Time  [0 reads].</font><br>
<font class="content"">(<a href="modules.php?name=News&amp;file=article&amp;sid=3240">comments?</a> | <a href="modules.php?name=News&amp;file=categories&amp;op=newindex&amp;catid=7">Gossip</a> | Score: 0)</font>

</td></tr></table></td></tr></table>
<br><br><br><table border="0" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFA8D3" width="100%"><tr><td>
<table border="0" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFA8D3" width="100%"><tr><td>
<table border="0" cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFA8D3" width="100%"><tr><td align="left">
<font class="storytitle" color="#FFFFFF"><b>Italians Do It Better.</b></font>
</td></tr></table></td></tr></table>

<table border="0" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="100%"><tr><td>
<a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=20"><img src="images/topics/live.gif" border="0" Alt="Live" align="right" hspace="10" vspace="10"></a>
<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><P>Here's the review of yesterday night show (<STRONG>MSG</STRONG>,<STRONG> New York City</STRONG>) by our friend <STRONG>Slyguy</STRONG>, who also took the pics below.</P>
<P>4th time watching the show and I'm not one bit tired of it! My crazy aunt and I (and another aunt and cousin 5 rows behind) had so much fun! My cousin is 9 years old and wants me to give her a bunch of <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> songs because she was mesmerized by <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>. </P>
<P><STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> was having a ball tonight and the crowd was deliriously excited throughout the show. <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> repeated what she did Sunday with <STRONG>"Don't Tell Me"</STRONG> by extending it a bit repeating the verse because she was enjoying it so much fun. When she paused to catch her breath and make the crowd scream, she bursted out laughing seeing the crowd react so wildly. </P>
<P>Instead of <STRONG>"Kabbalists Do It Better"</STRONG> t-shirts, <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> and the girls were wearing <STRONG>"Italians Do It Better"</STRONG> t-shirts! </P>
<P><STRONG>"Like A Prayer"</STRONG> still generates the biggest hysteria in the arena. You have to experience it yourself in person to understand how intense the hysteria is in the arena with everybody dancing, chanting, screaming and waving their arms in the air. So many people rushed the stage during <STRONG>"Like A Prayer"</STRONG>. </P>
<P><STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> gave <STRONG>NYC</STRONG> shout-outs throughout the show as usual and exclaimed that this <STRONG>NYC</STRONG> crowd was the best one so far (Personally I think Sunday night's crowd was a bit more intense) but I won't argue with her! She is so incredibly confident and at ease at the same time with her vocals and dancing. I love those moves they do while sitting on the stage at the beginning of <STRONG>"Holiday"</STRONG>.</P>
<P align=center><IMG src="/re/sluyguy/italians01.jpg" border=0></P>
<P align=center><IMG src="/re/sluyguy/italians02.jpg" border=0></P>
</font></div>
</td></tr></table>


</td></tr></table>


