<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><DIV class=postcolor><STRONG>Jeff Edelstein</STRONG> wrote in a worldwide exclusive, some excerpts that didn’t make it into the 957-page <STRONG>Clinton</STRONG> autobiography<BR>Here is a part on <B>Madonna</B><BR><BR>"That ‘<B>don’t ask, don’t tell’ </B>policy came out of a <B>late-night meeting I had with Madonna. She was still quite the pistol back in the early 90’s</B>. Anywho,<B> we were engaged in a little ‘Bosnia and Herzegovina’, if you catch my drift</B>. I asked her about <B>what would happen if someone found out about our ‘meeting</B>,’ and <B>she said not to worry</B>, she had a strict ‘don’t ask, don’t tell’ policy. Wasn’t quite sure what she meant, but the idea stuck."<BR></DIV>
