<font class="storytitle" color="#FFFFFF"><b>Photographer Cecil Beaton lived in Madonna's house</b></font>
</td></tr></table></td></tr></table>

<table border="0" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="100%"><tr><td>
<a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=6"><img src="images/topics/magazines.gif" border="0" Alt="Magazines" align="right" hspace="10" vspace="10"></a>
<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><SPAN id=postcolor><FONT color=#000000><STRONG>Ashcombe House</STRONG><BR>It was also in 1930 that he( Beaton) went to live in the then partly derelict Ashcombe House on the Wiltshire/Dorset border near Shaftesbury. He employed his talents to restore this house, which he rented over the next 15 years for around 50 UK pounds a month. It was a perfect weekend retreat for long parties for his friends, some of whom, including Salvador Dali and Rex Whistler, repaid his hospitality by painting murals. <BR><B>Beaton wrote a book 'Ashcombe: The Story of a Fifteen-Year Lease' about it that was published 4 years after he moved out in 1945. This six-bedroom house, together with a studio with seven more bedrooms, two farmhouses and three cottages with a surrounding downland estate of around 4.8 square kilometres with the best shooting in the county was sold to Madonna and Guy Ritchie for around 9 million UK Pounds (about 16 million US dollars) in 2001. </B><BR>source:photography.about.com</FONT> <!--Signature--><BR></SPAN>
</font></div>
</td></tr></table>


</td></tr></table>


